  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1232 PM CDT Fri Jul 31 2026\n\nMost of the CAMs show the convection pushing south of the area by\n00Z tomorrow afternoon, or at least within an hour or two after\nthat. Will not yet run POPs into Saturday night at this point but\nwill monitor to see if the activity lingers longer than expected.\n\nAfter tomorrow though, rain chances diminish pretty quickly. Upper\nhigh builds back into place. Its not the strongest upper ridge we\ncan see this summer, but its strong enough to inhibit most\nprecipitation chances for next week. After a little cool down\nbehind the weak front, temperatures will rebound back to near or a\nfew degrees above normal for next week.",
